    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '2 players (this variant). Also commonly 4 in partnerships or 4 individuals; rules are the same.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card pack (French suits, no jokers). Pişti uses the full deck: four cards are dealt face down to the centre, four to each player, and the remainder forms the stock; one centre card is turned face up to start the pile.',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card pack (French suits, no jokers). Pişti uses the full deck: four cards are dealt face down to the centre, four to each player, and the remainder forms the stock; one centre card is turned face up to start the pile.',
      dealing: "Dealer shuffles; player to dealer's left cuts. Dealer deals 4 cards face down to the center, then 4 to each player. Remaining cards form the stock. One of the four center cards is turned face up to start the pile (if it is a Jack, turn until a non-Jack). Player to dealer's right plays first. After all play their 4 cards, dealer deals 4 more to each from stock; repeat until stock is exhausted.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Each turn, play one card from your hand face up onto the center pile. If your card's rank matches the top card of the pile, you capture the whole pile; playing a Jack also captures the pile regardless of the top card. Otherwise your card stays on the pile. The first capture also takes the four face-down center cards. When everyone has played their four cards, the dealer deals four more to each from the stock; play continues until the stock is exhausted. The last team or player to make a capture takes any remaining cards. Score after each hand; first to 151 wins.",
